.\" halite-hub(8)
.Dd September 7, 2026
.Dt HALITE-HUB 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm halite-hub
.Nd the central service and the operator command line
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar arguments ...
.Op Fl -flag Ns = Ns Ar value ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the control plane.
It holds the enrollment authority, serves the state tree and the pillar,
dispatches jobs to nodes and records what they return, runs the event bus
and the reactor, and is the command line an operator drives the fleet
from.
.Pp
One process serves both: the same binary that runs
.Cm serve
is the one an operator types
.Cm run
into, and the second speaks to the first over the same mutually
authenticated transport a node uses.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "keys subcommand"
.It Cm serve
Run the control plane.
This is what the service unit runs.
With
.Fl -relay
it serves its own nodes and presents them to an upstream hub as one
client.
.It Cm keys Ar subcommand
The enrollment and key lifecycle: list requests, accept, reject, revoke,
and read a node's fingerprint.
.It Cm run Ar target Ar function Op Ar args ...
Run a function across the fleet.
.Fl -batch
makes the hub own the batch, so closing the terminal does not stop it.
.It Cm runner Ar function Op Ar args ...
Run a function on the hub itself rather than on a node.
.It Cm orch Ar subcommand
Orchestration, which runs on the hub and drives nodes in a defined order.
.It Cm jobs Ar subcommand
The job cache: list, look at one, resume a batch, or kill one in flight.
.It Cm policy Oo Cm show | test Oc
The role-based authorization policy, and what it decides for a given
principal, target and function.
.It Cm event Oo Cm listen | tags Oc
The event bus: follow it, or list the tags it carries.
.It Cm metrics
Print the Prometheus exposition.
.It Cm ssh Ar target Ar function Op Ar args ...
Run on a machine with no agent, by pushing the binary over SSH.
.It Cm doctor
Run the diagnostics of the specification's section 26.4 against this hub.
Changes nothing, and starts no listener, so it is safe on a hub that is
already running.
Exits non-zero only on a failure.
.It Cm migrate Ar tree
Audit an existing Salt tree and report what would and would not work.
.Sq lexicon:allow
.It Cm lint Ar path ...
Render and parse a file without executing anything in it.
.It Cm version
Print the build identity.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--config path"
.It Fl -help
Describe the program without running the command.
.It Fl -config Ar path
Configuration file.
Defaults to
.Pa hub.yaml
under the configuration root.
.It Fl -root Ar dir
Configuration root.
.It Fl -out Ar format
.Sy summary
(default) or
.Sy json .
.El
.Pp
.Cm serve ,
.Cm run ,
.Cm orch
and
.Cm ssh
each take a good many more; see
.Nm
.Fl -help .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/local/etc/halite/hub.yaml" -compact
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/halite/hub.yaml
Configuration on the BSDs.
.It Pa /etc/halite/hub.yaml
Configuration elsewhere.
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/halite/pki
The enrollment CA, and this hub's own certificate and key.
.It Pa /var/db/halite
Durable state on the BSDs;
.Pa /var/lib/halite
elsewhere.
Holds the job cache, the event bus and the key store.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Pp
.Cm run
exits non-zero when a node returned a failure, so a script does not have
to read the output to know.
.Cm doctor
exits non-zero only when a check fails, not when one warns.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Run a function across everything, a tenth of the fleet at a time:
.Pp
.Dl halite-hub run '*' test.ping --batch=10%
.Pp
Accept a node that has asked to enrol:
.Pp
.Dl halite-hub keys accept web1.example
.Pp
Ask what is wrong with this hub:
.Pp
.Dl halite-hub doctor
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr halite-node 8 ,
.Xr halite-api 8
.Pp
The command reference, the operations guide and the configuration
reference ship in
.Pa docs/
in the source tree.
